- "content": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.588), 20px);line-height:1.5\">Key indicators for Bangladesh&#8217;s development and humanitarian sector. Each figure shows its unit, period, geography and source.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Indicator</th><th>Value</th><th>Period</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Children reached by new World Bank primary education programme</td><td>About 26 million</td><td>Approved 6 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/07/world-bank-300-million-primary-education-bangladesh/\">World Bank, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>10-year-olds who cannot read a simple, age-appropriate text</td><td>About 50%</td><td>Latest World Bank estimate</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/07/world-bank-300-million-primary-education-bangladesh/\">World Bank, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Workers in the informal sector</td><td>About 84% (roughly 58 million people)</td><td>2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/05/world-bank-bangladesh-working-age-population-peaks-2045/\">World Bank, Demographic Change in South Asia</a></td></tr><tr><td>Year the working-age share of the population peaks</td><td>2045</td><td>Projection</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/05/world-bank-bangladesh-working-age-population-peaks-2045/\">World Bank, Demographic Change in South Asia</a></td></tr><tr><td>Garment minimum wage</td><td>Tk 12,500 a month (workers demand Tk 30,000)</td><td>Nov 2026; new scale due December</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/07/garment-unrest-eases-workers-return-tension-ashulia/\">The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Cost of the Health National Adaptation Plan</td><td>About US$1.4 billion (Tk 17,000 crore)</td><td>2026-2031</td><td><a href=\"/2026/10/29/climate-health-plan-needs-1-4-billion-over-five-years-study-finds/\">BRAC University C3ER study, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Secondary teachers with health education training</td><td>30.1% of those surveyed</td><td